Remove the "Use Google Translate" option from chrome://settings/languages.

ungoogled-chromium already neuters the translate backend (translation only
works if explicitly re-enabled via a command-line switch - see
core/ungoogled-chromium/toggle-translation-via-switch.patch), so the
"Google Translate" card on the languages page is a toggle for a service
Aerium doesn't talk to. Drop the card entirely.

The languages page composes three cards through a cr-view-manager, so the
element and its entry in switchViews() have to go together - leaving the
id in the list would make the view manager look up a view that no longer
exists. translate_page.{html,ts} itself is left in the build (still
imported, still listed in BUILD.gn); it is simply never instantiated.

--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/languages_page/languages_page_index.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/languages_page/languages_page_index.html
@@ -21,10 +21,6 @@
       languages="[[languages]]" route-path$="[[routes_.SPELL_CHECK.path]]">
   </settings-spell-check-page>

-  <settings-translate-page slot="view" id="translate" prefs="{{prefs}}"
-      languages="[[languages]]">
-  </settings-translate-page>
-
 <if expr="not is_macosx">
   <settings-edit-dictionary-page slot="view" id="editDictionary"
       data-parent-view-id="spellCheck" prefs="{{prefs}}"
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/languages_page/languages_page_index.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/languages_page/languages_page_index.ts
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@

   private showDefaultViews_() {
     this.$.viewManager.switchViews(
-        ['languages', 'spellCheck', 'translate'], 'no-animation',
+        ['languages', 'spellCheck'], 'no-animation',
         'no-animation');
   }
